<title>USA: Dawson-Samberg cuts Digicon stake.</title>
<headline>Dawson-Samberg cuts Digicon stake.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by Dawson-Samberg Capital Management Inc, a Southport, Conn., investment adviser, said it cut its stake in Digicon Inc to 602,400 common shares or 5.31 percent from 6.79 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said it sold a net of 23,600 common shares between June 21 and August 22 at prices ranging from $13.50 to $16.8393 per share.</p>
<p>Houston-based Digicon provides geophysical services operating seismic survey ships, land data acquisition crews and geophysical data processing centers.</p>
</text>
